# ═══ META-LESSONS ═══
L1: The 5th orphan was the deepest form — even the FUNCTION was missing, not just callsites. The "orphan counter" pattern has a spectrum: type-1 = field+init+function but 0 callsites (P3), type-2 = field+init but 0 function (5th orphan). Future audits should treat both as a standard finding class.

L2: Constitutional CODE constraints (type hints, typed errors, SRP, docstrings, no bare except) coexist with quick-delivery 1ed waves. The test count + quality didn't slip. This validates that constitutional discipline isn't a speed tax when applied incrementally.

L3: Python file-line indexing for YAML multi-line strings is brittle. The bug ate 1 row (formal-verify) which I had to restore mid-wave. Better approach: use a single-line sentinel + line-based read/write, OR use `awk` / `sed` for single-line replacements. Future waves should NOT use multi-line string slicing in Python.

L4: ALL P3-NO-OP orphan counters are now closed. The audit pattern (counter DEFINED + increment function CALLED) is a universal standard. The CAH oracle's spec_compat priors are now in sync with reality for 34/37 rows.
